| Lane | What it requires |
| :-- | :-- |
| M365 Technical Architect | M365 platform architecture, HLD/LLD, customer leadership, integrations |
| M365 Migration Architect | Discovery, migration tools, coexistence, cutover, rollback, reconciliation |
| Identity and Hybrid Architect | AD, Entra Connect, ADFS, Okta, SSO, tenant identity migration |
| Azure Cloud Security Engineer | Azure infrastructure, identity, NHI, networking, security operations, AI security |

Your current experience already gives you strong evidence for Microsoft 365 operations, Entra, automation, endpoint management, compliance, and customer/leadership work. The biggest new gaps are **large-scale migration delivery, Exchange hybrid, Teams/SharePoint architecture, migration tools, and formal architecture documentation**.[^52_3][^52_4][^52_6][^52_1]

## Required migration-factory labs

The repo should contain at least these practical factories:

### Factory 1: Google Workspace to Microsoft 365

- Assess domains, users, groups, aliases, mailboxes, Drive, calendars, and shared drives.
- Design identity and coexistence.
- Map Google groups to Microsoft 365 groups or security groups.
- Plan mailbox and Drive migration.
- Configure pilot users.
- Perform delta migration and cutover.
- Reconcile item counts, permissions, ownership, and failures.
- Produce a post-migration support plan.


### Factory 2: Microsoft 365 tenant-to-tenant

- Inventory users, domains, groups, apps, devices, mailboxes, SharePoint, OneDrive, Teams, and Power Platform.
- Design source and target identity.
- Plan domain and UPN transition.
- Handle cross-tenant access and coexistence.
- Re-register enterprise applications.
- Plan device re-enrollment and Intune migration.
- Execute migration waves.
- Validate and rollback.


### Factory 3: Hybrid Exchange to Exchange Online

- Assess Exchange versions, connectors, namespaces, certificates, mail flow, relay, public folders, and applications.
- Design hybrid configuration.
- Validate Autodiscover, OAuth, free/busy, mail flow, and relay.
- Migrate pilot mailboxes.
- Troubleshoot throttling, permissions, and delivery issues.
- Complete cutover and decommission safely.


### Factory 4: SharePoint, OneDrive, and Teams migration

- Inventory sites, teams, channels, owners, permissions, guest users, files, links, and inactive content.
- Resolve unsupported paths, invalid names, excessive permissions, and orphaned content.
- Map source permissions to target permissions.
- Migrate in waves.
- Reconcile content, permissions, sharing links, and ownership.
- Apply retention, sensitivity, DLP, and lifecycle policies.


## Required customer deliverables

Every migration lab must produce professional-services artifacts:

- Discovery questionnaire.
- Current-state assessment.
- Application and dependency inventory.
- Data classification matrix.
- Assumption and constraint register.
- Risk and issue register.
- High-Level Design.
- Low-Level Design.
- Migration runbook.
- Configuration checklist.
- Pilot plan.
- Test plan.
- Cutover plan.
- Rollback plan.
- User communication plan.
- Validation and reconciliation report.
- Operations manual.
- Standard operating procedures.
- Customer handover document.
- Post-migration review.

This is important because actual M365 architect roles explicitly expect HLDs, LLDs, build documentation, application handover, disaster-recovery documentation, configuration checklists, and SOPs—not just technical implementation.[^52_7][^52_1][^52_3]

## Revised 10-day sprint

The sprint should now be:


| Day | Focus |
| --: | :-- |
| 1 | Azure, Microsoft 365, AD, Entra, networking, and lab governance baseline |
| 2 | Exchange Online, mail flow, DNS, SPF/DKIM/DMARC, connectors, relay, hygiene |
| 3 | SharePoint, OneDrive, Teams, Groups, Viva, governance, and permissions |
| 4 | AD, Entra Connect, Cloud Sync, ADFS, hybrid identity, and federation |
| 5 | M365 discovery, assessment, inventory, dependency mapping, and migration design |
| 6 | Migration tools: native tools, BitTitan, Quest, ShareGate, Cloudiway, AvePoint concepts |
| 7 | Google Workspace-to-M365 and tenant-to-tenant migration factory |
| 8 | Exchange hybrid, SharePoint/OneDrive/Teams migration, cutover, rollback, reconciliation |
| 9 | Security, compliance, Defender, Purview, Intune, NHI, automation, and operations |
| 10 | Customer architecture pack, HLD/LLD, migration proposal, mock client workshop, and interview defense |

This is still intense, but it is now aligned to the market example you provided rather than just to Microsoft certification domains.

## Important honesty boundary

You should not claim hands-on experience with BitTitan, Quest, ShareGate, or Cloudiway until you have genuinely used them. The repo can contain:

- Product architecture research.
- Trial or sandbox exercises.
- Tool comparison.
- Migration design.
- Native-tool implementation.
- Simulated migration evidence.
- Honest “developing familiarity” labels.

That still helps you discuss the tools intelligently, but it does not turn research into production experience.

I would **not push the previous five-file scaffold yet**. It should be expanded first to include the M365 platform, migration factories, hybrid identity, consulting deliverables, and tool ecosystem above. I can replace that initial plan with the corrected market-aligned version and push it to the new repository after your confirmation.
